# promise: #817
# A hidden page (Live Calendar's reader for a Google Calendar favorite) runs its script once the page has loaded,
# though the page then loads a frame of its own, as a signed-in Google page does. The engine took the frame's load for
# a new page and left it uncommitted for good, so the reader never ran and every fetch "failed" after 25 s.
# late-frame.html adds its frame as soon as it has loaded; the hidden page is in the profile's own folder, as for a
# favorite in a profile's Favorites. With ?hold the frame answers 30 s late, so the page keeps loading: the script runs
# 5 s after the page committed anyway (Calendar's own script waits for its client). The engine itself keeps a tab with
# such a frame committed (engine 159.0.8154.45-9), which Instant Links and Easel live pages wait on.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
cra://debug?hiddenPageScript=${ORIGIN}/late-frame.html&profile=Default
wait 8
expect-log "GET /page\.html\?n=late-frame-child HTTP
expect-log hidden page script answered 127\.0\.0\.1:[0-9]+ after [0-7] s$
cra://debug?hiddenPageScript=${ORIGIN}/late-frame.html%3Fhold&profile=Default
wait 10
expect-log hidden page script answered 127\.0\.0\.1:[0-9]+ after [5-9] s$
cra://open?url=${ORIGIN}/late-frame.html%3Fn%3Dtab
wait 4
cra://debug?pageState=tab
expect-log page state tab: committed=1 loading=0$
